# App button styling

- Never introduce browser-default grey buttons or grey boxed action controls.
- Reuse an existing appropriate app button style. For lightweight actions, use transparent icon/text controls with the app's ink colours, not an unstyled `<button>`.
- For example, Home notebook shortcuts should use transparent icon/text actions, not native button chrome.
- Preserve visible keyboard focus, readable disabled/selected states, accessible labels for icon-only buttons, and at least 44px touch targets.
- Check the actual rendered controls at phone widths, including hover, focus and disabled states; a class name alone does not establish that a button is styled.
